.TH ENCLO-CONTAINER 1 "2026-06-07" "enclo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
enclo \- in-container enclo client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B enclo
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inside a container managed by
.BR enclo (1),
the
.B enclo
binary is the
.B enclo-container-client
program, installed at
.I /usr/local/bin/enclo
by the
.B container_client
module (enabled by default).
.PP
It provides three commands: fetching secrets from the
.B enclo-secrets
Unix socket, running commands with fetched secrets injected as environment
variables, and routing traffic through the enclo HTTPS proxy.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS get
Fetch one or more secrets and print them to stdout.
.PP
.B enclo get
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fINAMES\fR...]
.PP
At least one
.I NAME
or
.B \-\-group
is required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to the enclo-secrets Unix socket.
Default:
.IR /run/enclo/secrets.sock .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Client config file (for group definitions).
Default:
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/enclo/client.toml .
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-group " " \fIGROUP\fR
Fetch all secrets in the named group, as defined in the client config.
May be repeated or comma-separated.
.TP
.B \-\-env
Print secrets as shell
.B export
statements instead of a JSON object. Suitable for use with
.BR eval .
.PP
Secret names may include query-string parameters:
.IR "AWS_CREDENTIALS?profile=prod" .
Parameters are forwarded to the backend but stripped for access-control
pattern matching.
.SS run
Fetch secrets and execute a command with them set as environment variables.
.PP
.B enclo run
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fINAMES\fR...]
.B \-\-
.I CMD
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.PP
The
.B \-\-
separator is required. The command inherits the current environment
with the fetched secrets added.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to the enclo-secrets Unix socket.
Default:
.IR /run/enclo/secrets.sock .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Client config file.
Default:
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/enclo/client.toml .
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-group " " \fIGROUP\fR
Fetch all secrets in the named group.
.SS proxy
Run a command with
.B HTTP_PROXY
and
.B HTTPS_PROXY
set from
.BR $ENCLO_PROXY ,
or print those env vars.
.PP
.B enclo proxy
[\fB\-\-env\fR]
.PP
.B enclo proxy
.B \-\-
.I CMD
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.PP
.B $ENCLO_PROXY
is set by the
.B secrets
module when
.B mode = "explicit"
(the default). It contains the proxy URL including ephemeral basic-auth
credentials generated at container start.
.TP
.B \-\-env
Print
.B HTTP_PROXY
and
.B HTTPS_PROXY
as shell
.B export
statements.
Cannot be combined with a command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/enclo/secrets.sock
Default Unix socket path for the enclo-secrets service.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/enclo/client.toml
Client config file. Contains named groups of secrets.
.SH CLIENT CONFIG
The client config defines named groups of secrets:
.PP
.nf
[groups]
dev_tools = ["GITHUB_TOKEN", "NPM_TOKEN"]
aws_prod  = ["AWS_CREDENTIALS?profile=prod"]
.fi
.PP
Groups are referenced with
.BR \-g " / " \-\-group .
Deduplication is applied: a name appearing in both a positional argument and a
group is fetched only once.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Fetch a single secret as JSON
enclo get GITHUB_TOKEN

# Fetch multiple secrets
enclo get GITHUB_TOKEN NPM_TOKEN

# Fetch as shell exports
eval "$(enclo get --env GITHUB_TOKEN NPM_TOKEN)"

# Fetch a group from client.toml
enclo get --group dev_tools

# Fetch multiple groups (comma-separated)
enclo get --group dev_tools,aws_prod

# Run a command with a secret injected
enclo run GITHUB_TOKEN -- npm publish

# Run with a group
enclo run --group dev_tools -- make deploy

# Use an AWS profile
enclo run "AWS_CREDENTIALS?profile=prod" -- terraform apply

# Run curl through the secrets proxy
enclo proxy -- curl https://api.github.com/user

# Set proxy env vars for the current shell
eval "$(enclo proxy --env)"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR enclo (1),
.BR pass (1),
.BR gpg-agent (1)
.PP
Full documentation:
.I docs/container-commands.md
and
.I docs/secrets-configuration.md
in the enclo source tree.
